    "body": "Follows up [a review comment on #2439](https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/2439#discussion_r3830911397) asking whether `Either` isn't already built into OCaml. It is \u2014 twice \u2014 and ours was redundant, but the call sites turned out to want two different things.\n\n## Why ours had to go\n\n`src/util/Either.re` was four lines: `type t('l, 'r) = L('l) | R('r)` with `show`/`sexp`/`yojson`. Those derivations were dead \u2014 no `[@deriving]` type in the tree embeds an `Either.t`, which was the one plausible reason to keep our own over Core's.\n\nIt also **shadowed Core's**. Every library that uses it has `-open Core` in its dune, and every file that uses it also does `open Util`, which lands second, so `Core.Either` was unreachable without qualifying it.\n\n## What the call sites actually wanted\n\nOf 24 references, 20 were success-or-failure wearing the wrong constructors:\n\n| Site | Was | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Operators.re` (13) | `Either.t(Atom.t, bad_literal)` | `result(Atom.t, bad_literal)` |\n| `Atom.re` (3) | `Either.t('b, InvalidOperationError.t)` | `result('b, InvalidOperationError.t)` |\n| `Transition.re` (4) | `Either.L(return_value)` / `Either.R(error)` | `Ok` / `Error` |\n| `MatchedTyp.args` | `Either.t('a, int)` | `result(list(Typ.t), int)` |\n\n`result` puts the error direction in the type instead of leaving it to a convention about which side `R` is, and `MatchedTyp.args` gets a concrete ok type rather than the `'a` it was carrying.\n\nOnly **`Aba.split`** and its single caller **`Segment.split_by_matching`** genuinely partition \u2014 each element goes to the A-stream or the B-stream, and neither side is an error. Those take `Core.Either`'s `First`/`Second`.\n\n`src/util/Either.{re,rei}` and `Util`'s re-export of it are deleted. Removing the module made `open Util` dead in `MatchedTyp.re`, so that went too.\n\n`BuiltinsADT`'s `Either` is the Hazel-language type alias \u2014 a different thing entirely \u2014 and is untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `dune build @check --profile release` clean (no warnings)\n- `make dev` clean\n- `make test-quick`: 3556 tests pass\n\nNo behavior change is intended: this is a type-and-constructor rename, plus one type made less general.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UQDwH6tMjSMGSSykhjgQUP",
